ERROR REPORTS

We don't process error reports (see note on top of this file).

BUILDING AND RUNNING XV6

Run "make" to build the kernel, user programs, and disk images. The
Makefile defaults to the i686-elf- cross toolchain used for Mac development.
Override it with "make TOOLPREFIX=..." as needed; use TOOLPREFIX= for a
compatible native x86 ELF toolchain. HOSTCC selects the host compiler for mkfs.

Run "make qemu" for a graphical emulator or "make qemu-nox" for a terminal.
For debugging, run "make qemu-nox-gdb", then follow its GDB command from the
repository root. "make qemu-memfs" uses an in-memory filesystem.

LAYOUT

src/boot/       BIOS bootloader
src/kernel/     Kernel sources, internal headers, and linker script
src/user/       User programs, syscall stubs, and user library
src/include/    Shared kernel/user/host headers
tools/         Host utilities and build/debugging helpers
config/         GDB template and Bochs configuration
docs/           Upstream notes and legacy source-printing support
build/          All generated artifacts (ignored by Git)

The linked kernel is build/kernel.elf; objects live in build/kernel/,
build/user/, and build/boot/. Disk images live directly under build/.
"make clean" removes build/. "make print" stages a flat source copy under
build/printing/ for the upstream printing scripts (requires their original
printing dependencies). "make dist" creates a source copy in build/dist/;
"make dist-test" builds that copy, and "make tar" archives it.

Run "make format" or "make format-check" for C sources and headers. If
clang-format is not on PATH, set CLANG_FORMAT to its executable path, e.g.
"make format CLANG_FORMAT=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin/clang-format".
Include sorting is disabled because xv6 headers depend on include order.

BRANCHES

upstream preserves the original xv6 state. main contains the course baseline.
Create independent assignment branches from main, for example:

    git switch -c assignment/01 main

Keep assignment solutions out of main. Pin a semester baseline with a tag
when needed, so each assignment can start from the same revision.
